<article class="env-remark" id="0217">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0217">Remark <span data-tag="0217">1.2.2.4</span>.</a> The functor $X \mapsto \operatorname{Sing}_{\bullet }(X)$ carries limits in the category of topological spaces to limits in the category of simplicial sets (in fact, the functor $\operatorname{Sing}_{\bullet }$ admits a left adjoint; see Corollary <a data-tag="0022" href="/tag/0022">1.2.3.5</a>). It does not preserve colimits in general. However, it does carry coproducts of topological spaces to coproducts of simplicial sets: this follows from the observation that the topological $n$-simplex $| \Delta ^ n |$ is connected for every $n \geq 0$. </p>
</article>
